   "textLength": 515,
   "text": "Pre-qualification typically uses self-reported data to estimate the mortgage amount you may qualify for.\nPre-approval is usually the more involved step and provides a conditional loan offer, though the amount is not guaranteed.\nMost pre-qualifications use a soft credit inquiry, which won’t impact your credit score. Pre-approval requires a hard credit check that could temporarily lower your score.\n",
