   ],
   "textLength": 319,
   "text": "“Pre-qualification is a less involved step, with less verification steps completed in most cases,” said Phil Crescenzo Jr., Southeast division president of Nation One Mortgage Corporation. “A pre-qualification may be given with information entered from an applicant but not yet verified, such as with income or assets.”",
   "counts": {
    "links": 2,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.11,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 2286,
    "height": 108,
    "widthFraction": 0.41,
    "leftFraction": 0.26,
    "pageFraction": 0.24,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 13,
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "mntl-sc-block_8-0",
   "class": "comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 350,
   "text": "Using this information, the lender can determine the mortgage amount that you’d likely be eligible for, without doing a hard credit pull that could hurt your credit score. It might then issue a formal pre-qualification letter or simply state the amount it’s willing to lend you.1 This process can take anywhere from a few minutes to a couple of days.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 2422,
    "height": 137,
