   "textLength": 508,
   "text": "By pulling your credit, the lender can also better tailor the interest rate to suit your creditworthiness. Additionally, a pre-approved borrower may be able to qualify for an interest rate lock under certain circumstances, potentially in exchange for a fee. Most of the time, however, the lender will offer you a floating rate that’s tied to market conditions. You can still lock in a fixed rate afte",
