   "textLength": 399,
   "text": "You may be able to lower the interest rate you’re offered by taking certain steps before you apply for a mortgage. “I’ve seen way too many what I call ‘skeletons in the closet’ on credit reports. Many of these items can be incorrect, and some can be addressable,” Leibowitz added. “It’s better to start the process early so that there’s time to fix/address items that were unknown or not discussed.”",
