   "text": "In some cases, buyers can benefit from getting both a pre-qualification and pre-approval. If it’s still early in the homebuying process, a pre-qualification could be worth it in order to get a rough estimate of what you’ll be able to borrow. Then, once you’re ready for a more in-depth review of your finances, you could move forward with a pre-approval. In other cases, it could make sense to skip p",
